WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.440
Six islands, side by side.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.377
We have travelled from the central Pacific to the South Atlantic,

00:00:08.377 --> 00:00:10.492
the North Atlantic and the Arabian Sea.

00:00:11.592 --> 00:00:14.097
Their areas span four orders of magnitude,

00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:19.047
from Surtsey's one point three square kilometres to the Falklands' twelve thousand.

00:00:19.047 --> 00:00:24.236
Their ages span eight orders: from rocks a billion years old to land made in the 1960s.

00:00:25.336 --> 00:00:30.137
Notice that the inhabited islands are not necessarily the largest or most fertile.

00:00:30.137 --> 00:00:33.534
Access matters more: a landing place, a harbour, a lagoon.

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:34.705
And so does history.
